WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:12.000
Read paragraph 1. Put each idea into your own words.
Keep the details and qualifications. A warrior is one example; players might team up.
Then choose “Hide the text and recall paragraph 1”.

00:12.000 --> 00:19.000
The text is hidden. Silently explain paragraph 1 in your own words.
You do not need to type or record anything.
Choose “Check my recall” when you have finished.

00:19.000 --> 00:30.000
The text returns. An example recall says all players are warriors and team up.
That is too strong: “such as a warrior” is an example; “might band together” is a possibility.
Check the meaning you remembered, then choose “Next paragraph”.

00:30.000 --> 00:42.000
Read paragraph 2. Castronova notices an economy inside the game world.
Keep how players acquire goods and become wealthier as they play longer.
Then choose “Hide the text and recall paragraph 2”.

00:42.000 --> 00:49.000
The text is hidden again. Silently explain paragraph 2 only.
Keep the details and its connection to paragraph 1.
Choose “Check my recall” when you have finished.

00:49.000 --> 00:57.000
Check both paragraphs against what you remembered.
Paragraph 1 introduces a game world; paragraph 2 shows an economy inside it.
These paragraphs have not yet established real-money sales.

00:57.000 --> 01:00.000
Repeat one paragraph at a time: read, hide and recall, show the text and check.
A whole-passage recall is optional. Silent recall is not recorded or graded.
